{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SGRmfVpi7tKZy7UDMbsCRq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map — persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect\\\\n# Generated: 2026-05-17 by Paper Agent\\\\n# Target: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May cycle)\\\\n# Total entries: 39 (across 8 categories + technical foundation)\\\\n# All entries WebSearch-verified\\\\n\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  project: persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect\\\\n  target_venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-17\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 39\\\\n  categories:\\\\n    - production_safety_systems\\\\n    - multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    - discourse_analysis\\\\n    - computational_persuasion\\\\n    - jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    - red_teaming\\\\n    - annotation_artifacts\\\\n    - adaptive_attacks\\\\n    - technical_foundation\\\\n\\\\npapers:\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 1: Production Multi-Turn Safety Systems (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: inan2023llamaguard\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Llama Guard: LLM-based Input-Output Safeguard for Human-AI Conversations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Inan et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2312.06674\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational production safety classifier. Per-turn input/output guard\\\\n      that lacks multi-turn context modeling. DisPeD addresses this gap by\\\\n      modeling conversation-level persuasion trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: metallamaguard3_2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Llama Guard 3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Meta AI\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Meta AI (released with Llama 3.1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Latest iteration of Llama Guard with multilingual support and tool-use\\\\n      safety. Still operates per-turn without multi-turn trajectory modeling.\\\\n      Baseline comparison target for production safety systems.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: zeng2024shieldgemma\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"ShieldGemma: Generative AI Content Moderation Based on Gemma\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Zeng et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2407.21772\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Google's safety classifier suite (2B/9B/27B). Outperforms Llama Guard\\\\n      on public benchmarks. Demonstrates strong per-turn moderation but does\\\\n      not model multi-turn attack trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: han2024wildguard\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"WildGuard: Open One-Stop Moderation Tools for Safety Risks, Jailbreaks, and Refusals of LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Han et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2406.18495\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Allen AI's multi-task safety moderator (prompt harm + response harm +\\\\n      refusal detection). Reduces jailbreak ASR from 79.8% to 2.4% on\\\\n      single-turn attacks, but multi-turn evasion path remains open.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: anthropic2025constitutional\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Constitutional Classifiers: Defending against Universal Jailbreaks across Thousands of Hours of Red Teaming\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anthropic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2501.18837\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Anthropic's defense using synthetically-generated training data from\\\\n      constitutional rules. Reduces jailbreak ASR from 86% to 4.4%. Next-gen\\\\n      version uses exchange classifiers (input+output context). Production\\\\n      approach that our method complements with discourse-level analysis.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 2: Multi-Turn Jailbreak Defenses (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: deepcontext2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"DeepContext: Stateful Real-Time Detection of Multi-Turn Adversarial Intent Drift in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2602.16935\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      PRIMARY POSITIONING TARGET. Uses RNN over BERT embeddings to track\\\\n      generic semantic drift. Achieves F1=0.84. DisPeD differs by grounding\\\\n      representations in persuasion strategy classification rather than\\\\n      generic semantics, arguing persuasion structure is harder to evade\\\\n      than semantic content (Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: tong2025biid\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Bidirectional Intention Inference Enhances LLMs' Defense Against Multi-Turn Jailbreak Attacks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Tong et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2509.22732\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Combines forward request-based intention inference with backward\\\\n      response-based retrospection. Significantly reduces ASR on both\\\\n      single-turn and multi-turn attacks. DisPeD differs by using\\\\n      persuasion-grounded embeddings rather than intention inference.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: gguard2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"An Attention-Aware GNN-Based Input Defender Against Multi-Turn Jailbreak on LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2507.07146\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      GNN-based approach modeling conversation structure as graph.\\\\n      Evaluated against Crescendo and ActorAttack. Represents structural\\\\n      approach to multi-turn defense; DisPeD uses sequential (GRU) rather\\\\n      than graph modeling of persuasion trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: safedream2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"SafeDream: Safety World Model for Proactive Early Jailbreak Detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2604.16824\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      World-model approach with CUSUM detection and contrastive imagination.\\\\n      Achieves early detection (1.06-1.20 turns before compliance). Shares\\\\n      our goal of early detection but uses latent safety state prediction\\\\n      rather than persuasion strategy grounding.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: bullwinkel2025repeng\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Representation Engineering Perspective on the Effectiveness of Multi-Turn Jailbreaks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Bullwinkel et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2507.02956\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL MOTIVATION PAPER. Shows Crescendo keeps per-turn\\\\n      representations in \\\\\\\"benign\\\\\\\" region of representation space, explaining\\\\n      why per-turn defenses fail. This directly motivates DisPeD's approach\\\\n      of grounding representations in persuasion function rather than\\\\n      semantic content.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 3: Discourse Analysis in NLP (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: mann1988rst\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Rhetorical Structure Theory: Toward a Functional Theory of Text Organization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Mann and Thompson\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Text & Talk\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1988\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational discourse theory. RST's hierarchical text organization\\\\n      informs our modeling of persuasion strategy sequences as structured\\\\n      discourse rather than bag-of-features.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: prasad2008pdtb\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Penn Discourse TreeBank 2.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Prasad et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"LREC 2008\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2008\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Major discourse annotation resource. PDTB's approach to annotating\\\\n      discourse relations at the connective level parallels our annotation\\\\n      of persuasion strategies at the turn level.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: stolcke2000dialogueact\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Dialogue Act Modeling for Automatic Tagging and Recognition of Conversational Speech\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Stolcke et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Computational Linguistics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2000\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational dialogue act classification using HMM over sequential\\\\n      turns. Our GRU-based persuasion trajectory modeling is a modern\\\\n      analogue of this sequential discourse structure approach.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: austin1962speechacts\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How to Do Things with Words\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Austin, J. L.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Harvard University Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1962\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational speech act theory distinguishing locutionary,\\\\n      illocutionary, and perlocutionary acts. DisPeD operates at the\\\\n      illocutionary level (what the speaker intends to accomplish)\\\\n      rather than the locutionary level (what words are used).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: searle1969speechacts\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Speech Acts: An Essay in the Philosophy of Language\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Searle, J. R.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Cambridge University Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1969\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Extended Austin's speech act theory with systematic taxonomy.\\\\n      Our persuasion strategy taxonomy maps onto Searle's classification\\\\n      of illocutionary acts, providing theoretical grounding for\\\\n      treating persuasion as a functional category.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 4: Computational Persuasion Detection (4 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: habernal2016convincingness\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Which Argument Is More Convincing? Analyzing and Predicting Convincingness of Web Arguments Using Bidirectional LSTM\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Habernal and Gurevych\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2016\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Pioneering computational persuasion work predicting argument\\\\n      convincingness from text. Establishes that persuasive properties\\\\n      are computationally detectable from language, supporting our\\\\n      premise that persuasion strategies are extractable from turn\\\\n      representations.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: tan2016winningarguments\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Winning Arguments: Interaction Dynamics and Persuasion Strategies in Good-faith Online Discussions\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Tan et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"WWW 2016\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Analyzes persuasion dynamics in Reddit ChangeMyView. Shows timing,\\\\n      interaction patterns, and language features predict persuasion\\\\n      success. Supports our modeling of temporal persuasion trajectories\\\\n      as discriminative features.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: jaipersaud2025howdollmspersuade\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How Do LLMs Persuade? Linear Probes Can Uncover Persuasion Dynamics in Multi-Turn Conversations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Jaipersaud et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2508.05625\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL PRIOR WORK. Demonstrates persuasion dynamics are extractable\\\\n      from LLM turn-level representations via linear probes. Directly\\\\n      supports our premise that DeBERTa fine-tuned on persuasion taxonomy\\\\n      produces informative turn embeddings for trajectory modeling.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: cialdini2001influence\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Influence: Science and Practice\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Cialdini, R. B.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Allyn & Bacon (4th edition)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2001\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Six principles of \\\\n\\\\n... [截断: 省略 12216 字符，传 max_chars=0 获取完整内容]\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 24216, \\\"truncated\\\": true}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CpWnpkb89UmgUhiXhSzaDB","session_id":"663ec355-7f83-4836-8054-259e8989ba2c","uuid":"1fcf8b95-57c8-4c6c-adc2-6168e9315adb","timestamp":"2026-05-18T04:14:37.882Z"}
